---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Showcase from "../components/Showcase.astro";
---
<Base title="Aerie: a self-hosted knowledge base for IT teams"
      description="Aerie gathers your IT team's fixes, runbooks and know-how into one knowledge base, filed by team, versioned and searchable, on a server you own.">

<div class="hero">
  <div class="head">
    <h1>Everything your IT team knows, finally in one place.</h1>
    <p>Fixes hide in old email threads, chat history, sticky notes and the heads of your most experienced people. Aerie gets it all into one knowledge base, filed by team, versioned and searchable, on a server you own, so it's still there when someone is out sick, on vacation or moving on.</p>
  </div>
  <Showcase />
</div>

<section class="sec" id="spaces" aria-labelledby="spaces-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h2 id="spaces-h">Each team gets its own space</h2>
        <p class="lede">Infrastructure, network, identity, security: every team files its runbooks in its own space, with its own folder tree. Other teams don't see that space until someone gives them a role in it.</p>
        <p class="note">Roles go to people directly or to local groups. An Admin creates spaces and their Owners. Owners run the rest of their space's membership. Admins can add custom roles, which every space can use.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="ph">Roles in a space <span>per person or group</span></div>
        <table class="roles">
          <tr><th scope="row">Reader</th><td>Reads the pages in the space.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Contributor</th><td>Writes pages, and moves or deletes their own work.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Supervisor</th><td>Moves and deletes anyone's pages in the space.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Owner</th><td>Decides who else gets in, and at which role.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="rows">
      <div><dt>The editor</dt><dd>Code blocks, tables, images and attachments.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Every version kept</dt><dd>See what changed between any two versions, and restore an old one.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Drafts</dt><dd>Work on a page until it's right, then publish it.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Search that forgives typos</dt><dd>Find the spooler fix even when you type "spoolr".</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Export</dt><dd>Pages to PDF or Word, tables to CSV or Excel.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tags</dt><dd>Tag pages by server, app or topic, across folders.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="security" aria-labelledby="security-h">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2 id="security-h">Locked down by default</h2>
      <p class="lede">Runbooks hold server names, recovery steps and who to call. Aerie was designed around keeping them in the right hands, and it's tested against attack as it's built.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ul class="mech">
        <li><b>Sensitive spaces</b><span>Mark a space sensitive and it's closed to Admins too. An Admin who needs in uses emergency access, which is logged, and the space's Owners are told.</span></li>
        <li><b>A tamper-evident audit log</b><span>Each entry is hash-chained to the one before it, so an edited or deleted entry breaks the chain. Ship the log to your SIEM.</span></li>
        <li><b>Scoped API tokens</b><span>Tokens carry only the permissions you give them, and they expire.</span></li>
        <li><b>Built and tested to OWASP standards</b><span>Aerie is developed against the OWASP Top 10 and tested with OWASP methods. Automated tests try actions under every role and confirm the wrong ones are refused, and the running app is scanned for vulnerabilities, with findings fixed before release.</span></li>
        <li><b>Sign-in</b><span>One-time codes from an authenticator app at sign-in. Signing out ends every session for that account.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="panel audit">
        <div class="ph">Audit log <span>sample entries</span></div>
        <div class="wide">
          <table class="mono">
            <tr><td>2026-11-12 22:41</td><td>admin.pat</td><td>Emergency access: Security Operations</td><td>9f3c…e1a0</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-11-12 22:41</td><td>system</td><td>Owners notified: Security Operations</td><td>2b77…09cd</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-11-12 22:58</td><td>admin.pat</td><td>Viewed: Ransomware Playbook</td><td>c41e…7f52</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2 id="install-h">Runs on your server</h2>
      <p class="lede">No cloud service sits behind Aerie. Your pages stay on hardware you control, and it's free to self-host.</p>
      <p class="note">An install guide comes with the first release. Until then, the live demo runs the current build.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hosts">
      <div>
        <h3>Windows Server</h3>
        <ul><li>Runs under IIS</li><li>SQL Server database</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Docker</h3>
        <ul><li>One container image</li><li>A single SQLite file, or SQL Server</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="roadmap" aria-labelledby="roadmap-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="roadmap-h">Where it's headed</h2>
    <p class="lede">Aerie is in development. Here's what works today, what's being built, and what's planned.</p>
    <div class="road">
      <div>
        <h3>Works today</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Team spaces with roles, custom roles and local groups</li>
          <li>Spaces private, open to signed-in users, or open to anyone</li>
          <li>Sensitive spaces and emergency access</li>
          <li>One-time sign-in codes</li>
          <li>Version history, drafts, recycle bin</li>
          <li>Search, clickable tags, PDF and Word export</li>
          <li>Audit log with filters, API token use and SIEM shipping</li>
          <li><b>AI import:</b> drop in files, review each draft page before it's saved</li>
          <li><b>AI format and assist</b> in the editor</li>
          <li><b>Application inventory:</b> apps and versions per server, linked to pages</li>
          <li>Theme colors for Day and Night, set by an Admin</li>
          <li>Plugins with their own screens and data</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="now">
        <h3>In progress</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The first release, with an install guide</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Planned</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Page comments,</b> moderated by the space's Supervisors and Owners.</li>
          <li><b>Page ratings,</b> including a "This solved my problem" button.</li>
          <li><b>Smarter search</b> with AI.</li>
          <li><b>Azure Blob</b> for file storage.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="close" aria-labelledby="close-h">
  <h2 id="close-h">See it with real pages</h2>
  <p>The demo has four IT team spaces and about 290 pages, running the current build.</p>
  <a class="btn" href="https://demo.aeriekb.com">Live Demo</a>
</section>

</Base>
